<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enna-Dagan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">24th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/24th-century-bce">24th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enna-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagan">Dagan</a> was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in the twenty-fourth century BCE. He is known chiefly from a letter found in the archives of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebla">Ebla</a> in which he recounts the campaigns of Mari's kings, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iblul-il">Iblul-Il</a>, against towns in Ebla's sphere of influence. The letter shows Mari's dominance over Ebla at the time, when Ebla delivered large amounts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and gold to Mari.</p></div>
